Description: docked-manager: keep the close button in phone mode
 Undocked, phosh set the window button layout to "appmenu:", taking away the
 close button.  A device whose only keys are a keypad has no Escape, and its
 back key (XF86Back) closes no GTK dialog, so a dialog such as Settings'
 "Modem Details" could not be left at all.  Phone mode now sets
 "appmenu:close".
Author: e5-linux
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/src/docked-manager.c
+++ b/src/docked-manager.c
@@ -299,7 +299,10 @@
   if (enable)
     g_settings_reset (self->wm_settings, WM_KEY_LAYOUT);
   else
-    g_settings_set_string (self->wm_settings, WM_KEY_LAYOUT, "appmenu:");
+    /* Keep the close button: a keypad phone has no Escape, and its back key
+     * (XF86Back) closes no GTK dialog, so without it a dialog such as
+     * Settings' "Modem Details" cannot be left at all. */
+    g_settings_set_string (self->wm_settings, WM_KEY_LAYOUT, "appmenu:close");
 
   /* we could bind one boolean property via g_settings_bind but that would spread
    * mode setup over several places */
